  "date": "2022-03",
  "notes": [
   "Scanned (raster) plots, traced from hand-placed hints. Print film: the curves describe the film as a print stock (exposure from a negative, not from a scene).",
   "Characteristic curves (page 4, 'Sensitometric Curves'): x axis is absolute log exposure in lux-seconds as printed (-3.0 to 3.0); exposure 1/500 sec tungsten plus KODAK Heat Absorbing Glass No. 2043 (plus Series 1700 filter), process ECP-2D, Status A densitometry (no colour temperature is printed for this exposure; the MTF plot on the same page says tungsten 3200 K). Here the B curve is the leftmost (fastest), then G, then R; all three reach a common maximum density of about 4.1, B and G merge into the R plateau near log exposure 1.9-2.0 and only R is drawn to about 2.6. R and G toes lie within about 0.04 density of each other and overlap with the plot's bottom frame line near D 0.03 to 0.1; B starts at log exposure -1.0, G and R at about -0.7.",
   "Spectral sensitivity (page 5): exposure tungsten 1/50 sec, process ECP-2D, D=1.0; y is log sensitivity (reciprocal of exposure in erg/cm2 required to produce the specified density) as printed. b = yellow-forming layer (drawn from 360 nm; it dips to -0.3 at 400 nm and peaks at about 0.65 near 462 nm), g = magenta-forming layer (drawn only from 450 nm, starting at -1.75, peak about -0.12 at 550 nm), r = cyan-forming layer (drawn from 585 nm, peak about -1.1 near 700 nm). An unlabelled pair of steep curves between 365 and 405 nm (starting near -0.75 and falling below -3.0 at about 390 to 405 nm) is not traced. The plot has thick black grid lines, so the curves are bridged across them. The sharp apex of g at 550 nm sits on the 550 nm grid line and is lost with it: the traced g is about -0.33 at 545-555 nm while the drawn apex is about -0.18.",
   "Spectral dye density (page 5): process CP-2D (as printed on the plot), y is diffuse spectral density, the dyes are 'normalized to form a visual neutral density of 1.0 for a xenon-arc viewing illuminant' (yellow peak about 0.82 near 445 nm, magenta about 0.88 near 540 nm, cyan about 1.07 near 655 nm; the curves are NOT peak-normalised to 1.0 although the text says peak-normalized); `neutral` is the plotted 'Visual Neutral' curve (the sum). The printed wavelength labels of this plot are squeezed (labels 250 ... 750 span less than the plot): the axis is calibrated from the frame and tick marks (frame 250 nm at the left, 750 nm at the right, ticks every 50 nm), which put the dye peaks at plausible wavelengths. The yellow and cyan curves both start at about 0.27 at 350 nm, magenta at about 0.09. Curves are drawn from 350 nm to 750 nm; m is traced only to 675 nm and y to 600 nm, beyond that they lie in the bottom frame line (density below about 0.03).",
   "Not traced: modulation transfer function and diffuse rms granularity plots (page 4); the rms granularity plot is on a Sigma-D scale and is not recorded in meta.grain."
  ]
 }
